      "value": "@{58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c|full_name}: I don't get hitches/loading screens when someone else joins the world or switches avatars, only when I do, and I'd rather get a 1 second long hitch then 10 seconds of standing there as a blue man waiting to load.\n\nThe point isn't whether or not one tradeoff is better than the other though. This change should be reverted because it's not the right solution. It fixes one problem, but causes two other problems in return (10 second long avatar load times and can't fix the override stuck bug anymore). This game is already plagued with new bugs every update due to decisions like this. Please, if you're going to fix something don't break something else. I don't understand why this compromise even exists when we didn't have to deal with either of these issues a few months ago.\n\nI know that if this change goes through to live, it will never be looked at again in terms of fixing the avatar load times and then we'll just have another new issue on our hands brought on by a new patch that will never get fixed. Please, do not push this update to live as it is right now, it's just replacing old aggravation with new aggravation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
