      "value": "@{58d2df84430f4652e88c5666|full_name}: That's not going to work anymore. Which is wonderful news for FBT people who sometimes get their face gestures stuck while calibrating if they have an override on the grip buttons used to calibrate like myself. Now that means we'll have to switch back and forth and try to recalibrate it. And then if they get stuck again later, say you sit on a chair accidentally or something, you've gotta switch back and forth again for another 20 seconds, and then you run the risk of screwing up the calibration again, forcing you to switch back and forth yet again for another 20 seconds. Hell if you really screw it up you could be trying to switch avatars back and forth for an entire minute!\n\nYou can see why this issue would become extremely aggravating extremely quickly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
