      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Pretty much. The issue I have with the patch is mostly that it breaks two things while only fixing one thing in return. I also still don't understand why we have to have this trade-off when we didn't have any of these issues before in terms of loading screens while switching avatars or long avatar load times. You told me before it's just the way things have to be now for whatever reason, and I'll just have to accept that answer, but it's still rather disappointing that we're unable to go back to what worked in the past for whatever reason.\n\nBack to the issue though, there are only two workarounds for the gesture fix issue right now, which is either mute/block by default, or switch avatars back and forth. This patch removes the ability to mute/block by default as a fix, and makes avatar switching take much longer. It's taking an annoying bug and making it 10x more annoying and harder to deal with. And like I said as well a lot of times the face gesture bug gets stuck while calibrating, which if you're in FBT you do every time you switch into a new avatar, so having it get stuck there means more avatar switching, more standing there as a blue man waiting to try and fix it again, etc. etc.\n\nSo basically this fix creates more nuisances while only fixing one nuisance, which is why I'm against implementing it as it currently is. I understand that from a development standpoint getting rid of the loading screens is obviously more of a priority than fixing the stuck face gesture bug, but fixing one common bug while making another common bug 10x more annoying doesn't seem like the right fix to me.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
